1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,450
How to Build a New Habit.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:06,700
The most common mistake in habit formation is starting too large.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:15,650
BJ Fogg’s research demonstrates that tiny habits — behaviors so small they require almost no motivation — are far more likely to stick.

4
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:18,412
Flossing begins with one tooth.

5
00:00:18,412 --> 00:00:21,437
Reading begins with one paragraph.

6
00:00:21,437 --> 00:00:26,600
The key is attaching the new habit to an existing routine, which serves as a trigger.

7
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:30,075
Consistency matters infinitely more than intensity.

8
00:00:30,075 --> 00:00:36,100
A tiny habit performed daily rewires the brain more effectively than grand effort done sporadically.

9
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:40,737
Once the small habit becomes automatic, it can be expanded gradually.

10
00:00:40,737 --> 00:00:44,587
This method bypasses the brain’s resistance to change.

11
00:00:44,587 --> 00:00:47,400
Running a marathon is intimidating.

12
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:50,287
Putting on running shoes is achievable.

